  "verbalization": "Zidovudine is likely to interact with Slc22a7 through a mechanism involving organic anion transport. The evidence suggests that Zidovudine binds to Slc22a11 or Slc22a6, which are both involved in organic anion transport. This transport process is mediated by Slc22a7, as these proteins participate in the transport of organic anions and zwitterions. The binding of Zidovudine to these transporters may alter their function, potentially affecting the uptake or efflux of organic anions, including those of Zidovudine itself. The cumulative scores from the three paths indicate a plausible, though moderate, relationship between Zidovudine and Slc22a7, supported by the shared role of these transporters in anion transport. The mechanism is biologically plausible, as Slc22a7 is a well-characterized member of the Slc22 family, involved in the transport of various organic molecules. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Zidovudine and Slc22a7, though further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the exact nature of the interaction.",
